## Important license notes for downstream users

This MIT license covers **the source code in this repository only**.

The following third-party components have **different licenses** that you must
respect separately:

### Pretrained weights (downloaded by scripts/download_weights.py)

| Component | License | Commercial use note |
|---|---|---|
| Ultralytics YOLO11 / YOLO26 base | **AGPL-3.0** | For commercial deployment, you MUST either open-source your entire service under AGPL OR purchase an Ultralytics Enterprise license. https://www.ultralytics.com/license |
| PARSeq base recognizer | MIT | Free for commercial use |
| Real-ESRGAN realesr-general-x4v3 | Apache-2.0 | Free for commercial use |
| PaddleOCR PP-OCRv4 mobile | Apache-2.0 | Free for commercial use |
| ByteTrack / supervision | MIT | Free for commercial use |

### Datasets (referenced in DATA_PROVENANCE.md)

| Dataset | License |
|---|---|
| CCPD | Academic use only — cite Xu et al. 2018 |
| Roboflow Universe sets | Per-dataset, mostly CC-BY-4.0 |
| UFPR-ALPR | Academic — cite Laroca et al. 2018 |
| AOLP | Academic |

**The Ultralytics AGPL is the only license trap in the stack.** If you intend
to deploy ANPR-India commercially, you need an Ultralytics Enterprise license
to use YOLO11/YOLO26. PARSeq, Real-ESRGAN, and PaddleOCR are all permissive.

### Privacy compliance (India)

License plate strings are personal data under India's Digital Personal Data
Protection Act 2023 (DPDP Act). For any deployment targeting Indian users:

- Do not store raw plate images beyond the inference call
- Store plates as salted hashes if you need historical queries
- Document data subject access rights in your service README
- Blur faces in any demo / marketing material (ANPR cameras capture more than plates)
- ANPR is surveillance-adjacent technology — handle with care

This software does not include legal advice. Consult a qualified lawyer for
DPDP Act compliance before deployment.
